	(text "DIY-Thermocam V4.0 Lepton carrier"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3 3)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "837370c7-0b2f-4ad7-a280-c4949476d86d")
	)
	(text "Replaces the FLIR Lepton Breakout Board V2.0 and the right-angle adapter. It sits on four 12 mm sleeves behind the main board;\nJ101 plugs straight into J2 and J102 holds the Lepton 3.5, 3.1R or 2.5."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 33.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1503e931-f929-44ac-a396-9d2bc6030538")
	)
	(text "Circuit follows FLIR's Breakout V2 (250-0577-00 rev 110) with parts JLCPCB stocks:\n- VDDC 1.2 V from a TLV62568 buck (breakout: AAT1146).\n- VDD 2.8 V and VDDIO 3.0 V from ME6211 LDOs (breakout: FT533GA, both 2.8 V). VDDIO 3.0 V is inside the\n  2.8-3.1 V range and keeps the 3.3 V I2C pull-ups and SPI levels further from the VDDIO + 0.6 V limit.\n- 25 MHz SiTime clock with 2 ns edges (the Lepton needs 3.4 ns or faster). Reset delay 47k/1uF (about 30 ms;\n  the breakout uses 10k) clears the clock's 5 ms start-up; same 100k PWR_DWN_L pull-up. I2C pull-ups on main board.\n- GPIO0-2 and VPROG stay open, as FLIR's datasheet requires.\n- J101 keeps the breakout's pin numbers but carries only what J2 uses: 5 V, GND, I2C, SPI and VSYNC.\n  The rails, the 25 MHz clock, RESET_L and PWR_DWN_L stay on the carrier (the breakout also brought them out).\n- No jumpers and no input diode: the carrier only takes 5 V from J2."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 215.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "73d5b7ca-eab6-481f-90da-2544a52e7349")
	)
